        <webservice>//bar.utoronto.ca/eplant/cgi-bin/plantefp.cgi?datasource=rice_single_cell&amp;</webservice>
        <info>
            <li>DRAFT / placeholder datasource: this manuscript (Robertson, Maqsood, Pasha, Provart &amp; Wilkins, in prep.) is not yet published and has not been assigned a GEO accession (the draft methods cite it as "GSExxxxxx"). <b>Every <code>sample</code> name below is a non-resolving placeholder</b> (format <code>PENDING-GEO_&lt;condition&gt;_rep&lt;n&gt;</code>) and must be replaced with the real GSM accessions once the series is deposited.</li>
            <li>Single-nuclear RNA-seq (snRNA-seq) atlas of developing <i>Oryza sativa</i> cv. Nipponbare third leaves, comparing well-watered (WW) control against mild drought (MD), moderate drought (ModD), mild salinity (MS), and moderate salinity (ModS) treatments (10x Genomics Chromium 3&#x2019; v3.1, NovaSeq 6000, ~16,000 nuclei targeted per library).</li>
            <li>The draft reports a total of 11 sequenced libraries across the 5 conditions but does not give a per-condition replicate breakdown in the available text (Table S1 is referenced but not included in this draft). <b>This file assumes 2 placeholder replicates per condition (10 total) as a structural default &#x2014; please correct replicate counts/names once Table S1 / the GEO submission is finalized.</b></li>
            <li>Cell types are pseudobulk-summed nuclear counts (CPM-like: counts per cell type per condition, normalized to total counts in that cell type &#x00d7; 10,000) computed with Seurat v5, per the draft's Section 4.9 methods.</li>
            <li>Cell-type groups below are the 10 colourable cell-type groups actually present as ids in <code>rice_template_ow.svg</code>. <b>Note:</b> the draft text states the pseudobulk eFP view uses "11 distinct mature cell types" &#x2014; only 10 are drawn in this SVG, so an 11th cell type (e.g. Procambium, mentioned elsewhere in the draft as a distinct vascular population) may be missing from the template or merged into one of the above; please reconcile with Nicholas/Sean before this goes live.</li>
            <li><b>Tissue ids below are the literal, verbatim <code>id</code> attributes from <code>rice_template_ow.svg</code></b> (e.g. <code>Bundle.Sheath-97</code>), resolved to their condition by computing each group's path centroid and matching it to the panel quadrant carrying that condition's <code>aria-label</code> text. The Well Watered control is drawn twice in the template (once alongside the drought panels, once alongside the salinity panels) and neither of its two panels carries an <code>aria-label</code>, so both of its ids per cell type were resolved by position (left column of each row) rather than by label text &#x2014; this is the same root cause flagged earlier for why Well Watered failed to colour in the live tool, now resolved here by explicit position-based assignment.</li>
            <li>Link URLs are placeholders (<code>PENDING_DOI_NOT_YET_PUBLISHED</code>) since no DOI exists for an unpublished manuscript; update once a preprint or accepted-article DOI is available.</li>
        </info>

